-- ====================================================================================================
-- cases-seat questions of seat person from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-cases-seat-person: the cases of the questions in P0-seat-person.l4: the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Regulation before the file was run and is written beside its assertion with the words that license it;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. A failing assertion is a finding, never an expectation to edit.
-- Dates the cases stand on: 31 July 2024 (the day before entry into force), 1 August 2024, 1 and 2 February 2025 (Chapter I), 26 and 27 July 2026 (each side of the Omnibus),
-- 1 and 2 August 2026 (the general date), 2 December 2026, 2 August 2027, 2 December 2027, 2 August 2028, 2 August 2030, 31 December 2030, as each function needs.
-- A MIRROR comment marks a case whose facts are asked, with the same answer, in the case file of another seat (the Guide, section 3).
-- A #TRACE is preceded by its -- EXPECT line (FULFILLED, BREACH or OPEN: the obligation still pending). The clock of a trace is the number of days since the day the rule counts from.
-- Assertions: 55. Traces: 0.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`

-- Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked
-- 1 January 2024, before the Regulation exists: JUST FALSE, the Regulation has not entered into force (Art 113, first paragraph: "on the twentieth day following that of its publication")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 1 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 31 July 2024, the day before entry into force: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 31 7 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 August 2024, in force but Chapter I applies only from 2 February 2025: JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 1 February 2025, the day before Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST FALSE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, the day Chapter I applies (Art 113(a)): JUST TRUE
-- MIRROR Art 113(a): whether Chapter I applies, asked from every seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 2 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 26 July 2026, the text as enacted still in force: JUST TRUE (as enacted point (a): "Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 26 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (point (a) as replaced keeps 2 February 2025 for Chapters I and II)
#ASSERT `Under Article 1, as a person affected by an AI system, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` (Date 27 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 2(1): does the Regulation apply to me?`

-- Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person located in the Union
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(g) answers (the affected person located in the Union); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person located in the Union` (Date 1 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, an affected person located in the Union: JUST TRUE ("affected persons that are located in the Union")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(g) answers (the affected person located in the Union); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
-- MIRROR Art 2(1)(b) and (g): a deployer in the Union and a person affected by its AI system, located in the Union
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person located in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, a person located in a third country: NOTHING (limited by "that are located in the Union")
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` EQUALS NOTHING; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(g) answers (the affected person located in the Union); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person located in the Union` (Date 2 2 2025) `Established or located in a third country` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (limb (g) was not changed)
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE; the question was retitled to ask what Art 2(1)(g) answers (the affected person located in the Union); the facts and the expected value are unchanged
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(1)(g), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to me as an affected person located in the Union` (Date 27 7 2026) `Established or located in the Union` EQUALS JUST TRUE


§ `Article 2(7): personal data law (the Omnibus changed the provisions reserved)`

-- Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to my personal data
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to my personal data` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, personal data processed in connection with the Regulation: JUST TRUE ("Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation")
-- MIRROR Art 2(7) first sentence: personal data processed in connection with the Regulation, asked from the provider, deployer and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to my personal data` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 2 February 2025, no such processing: NOTHING (limited by "personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to my personal data` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST TRUE (the first sentence is the same in both texts)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications apply to my personal data` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE 9 "" 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026 (text as enacted), Article 10(5): NOTHING ("without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59" as enacted)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE 10 "" 5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 26 July 2026, Article 9: JUST FALSE (not reserved)
-- MIRROR Art 2(7) second sentence: the same provision asked from the provider, deployer and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE 9 "" 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 26 July 2026, not one of the four instruments: NOTHING (the sentence names those four instruments)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 26 7 2026) FALSE 9 "" 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026 (text as amended), Article 4a: NOTHING ("Without prejudice to Articles 4a and 59")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE 4 "a" 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, Article 10 paragraph 5: JUST FALSE (no longer reserved as amended)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE 10 "" 5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 27 July 2026, Article 9: JUST FALSE (not reserved)
-- MIRROR Art 2(7) second sentence: the same provision asked from the provider, deployer and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE 9 "" 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 27 July 2026, not one of the four instruments: NOTHING
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(7), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation affect the Union data protection instruments through the provision I name` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE 4 "a" 0 EQUALS NOTHING


§ `Article 2(9): other Union legal acts on consumer protection and product safety`

-- Under Article 2(9), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation prejudice the rules of another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(9), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation prejudice the rules of another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a Union legal act on consumer protection or product safety: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation is without prejudice to the rules laid down by other Union legal acts related to consumer protection and product safety")
-- MIRROR Art 2(9): the rules of another Union legal act, asked from the person seat (consumer protection) and the manufacturer seat (product safety)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(9), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation prejudice the rules of another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, another kind of act: NOTHING (the sentence speaks of acts on consumer protection and product safety)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(9), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation prejudice the rules of another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 9 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(9), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation prejudice the rules of another Union legal act related to consumer protection or product safety` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(10): deployers who are natural persons in a purely personal non-professional activity`

-- Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a natural person deployer in a purely personal non-professional activity: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not apply to obligations of deployers who are natural persons using AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity")
-- MIRROR Art 2(10): a natural person who deploys an AI system for a purely personal non-professional activity, asked from the deployer seat and from the person seat
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, a natural person using the system in a professional activity: NOTHING (limited by "purely personal non-professional activity")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a deployer that is not a natural person: NOTHING (limited by "deployers who are natural persons")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 10 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(10), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation apply to the obligations of a deployer who is a natural person using AI systems for a purely personal non-professional activity` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 2(11): laws and collective agreements more favourable to workers`

-- Under Article 2(11), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation preclude a law or collective agreement that is more favourable to me as a worker
-- 1 February 2025, Chapter I has not begun to apply, so nothing is covered (Art 113(a): Chapters I and II "shall apply from 2 February 2025")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(11), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation preclude a law or collective agreement that is more favourable to me as a worker` (Date 1 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 2 February 2025, a more favourable law or collective agreement: JUST FALSE ("This Regulation does not preclude the Union or Member States from maintaining or introducing laws, regulations or administrative provisions which are more favourable to workers ...")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(11), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation preclude a law or collective agreement that is more favourable to me as a worker` (Date 2 2 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 2 February 2025, not more favourable to workers: NOTHING (the sentence speaks of provisions "more favourable to workers")
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(11), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation preclude a law or collective agreement that is more favourable to me as a worker` (Date 2 2 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 27 July 2026, the text as amended: JUST FALSE (paragraph 11 was not changed)
#ASSERT `Under Article 2(11), as a person affected by an AI system, does the Regulation preclude a law or collective agreement that is more favourable to me as a worker` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE


§ `Article 3(1): is it an AI system?`

-- Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system
-- all four elements met: TRUE ("a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy ... and that ... infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs ... that can influence physical or virtual environments")
-- MIRROR Art 3(1): the same software asked from the provider, deployer and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- not machine-based: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- no autonomy: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- does not infer how to generate outputs: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- outputs cannot influence physical or virtual environments: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(1), as a person affected by an AI system, is the system that affects me an AI system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`

-- Under Article 3(8), as a person affected by an AI system, am I an operator
-- the seat's role is passed as the keel's `Role`: FALSE (the definition says "means" and the list ends with the distributor): the role of this seat is not an operator
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(8), as a person affected by an AI system, am I an operator` EQUALS FALSE


§ `Article 3(49): serious incident`

-- Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident
-- an incident leading to death or serious harm to health: TRUE (point (a))
-- MIRROR Art 3(49): the same event asked from the provider, deployer, importer, distributor and person seats
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- an incident leading to a serious and irreversible disruption of critical infrastructure: TRUE (point (b))
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- an incident leading to the infringement of fundamental rights obligations: TRUE (point (c))
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- an incident leading to serious harm to property or the environment: TRUE (point (d))
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- not an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system: FALSE (the definition says "means")
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- an incident that leads to none of the four consequences: FALSE
#ASSERT `Under Article 3(49), as a person affected by an AI system, is the event a serious incident` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE


